      "final_text": "Done. `check_candidate` returns `VERIFIED` and `verify_passport` reproduces it.\n\n## Fix\n\nThe bug: `VyperSqrt.sqrt` returned the last Babylonian iterate `z`, which can sit above the true root (e.g. raw `9999999998` \u2192 `9999999999`). In [candidate/Solution.lean](<workspace>/candidate/Solution.lean) I defined `sqrt` as the deployed loop plus the v0.4.1 correction \u2014 the smaller of the last two iterates:\n\n```lean\ndef sqrt : SqrtFn := vyperSqrtWith (fun y z => if y < z then y else z)\n```\n\nThis satisfies `DeployedLoop` by construction (`rfl`), and `req_sqrt_neg_reverts` by the `x < 0` guard.\n\n## Proof\n\nThe loop on non-negative decimals is Newton iteration `newton (x\u00b710\u00b9\u2070) z` from seed `x/2 + 5\u00b710\u2079`, so the result must be `\u230a\u221a(x\u00b710\u00b9\u2070)\u230b`. Proved in stages, reusing `ProofForgeFin.Sqrt`:\n\n- Seed above the root via AM-GM (`four_mul_le_sq`); quotients bounded by `s+2`; iterates stay in `[s, seed+1]` and every `a/t + t` sum stays in decimal range, so the loop never reverts (`req_sqrt_total`).\n- Halving bound gives error \u2264 3 after 167 steps, \u2264 2 after one more, then `newton_le_sqrt_add_one` (needs `s \u2265 10\u2075`) puts step 169 at `s` or `s+1`; that set is invariant, so steps 255\u2013256 are there and `min_newton_eq_sqrt` gives exactly the root.\n- A fuel-indexed simulation (`sim_aux`) ties the actual `loop` to these Nat iterates, handling early exit via the fixed-point lemma and the `x = seed` case explicitly.\n- The Int bridge casts `Nat.sqrt` bounds (`Nat.sqrt_le`, `Nat.lt_succ_sqrt`) to the raw-value statements for `req_sqrt_not_above` / `req_sqrt_not_below`; negative inputs are vacuous via `req_sqrt_neg_reverts`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build Solution`: compiles, no `sorry`.\n- `check_candidate`: `VERIFIED` \u2014 all 5 requirements proved, accepted by all six kernels, axioms limited to `propext`/`Quot.sound`/`Classical.choice`, 2001/2001 property tests pass.\n- Passport `.proofforge/passport-001.json` (`sha256 06e535",
